## DeprecatedTag

**Severity:** warning | **Type:** LiquidHtml | **Aliases:** `DeprecatedTags`

This check is aimed at eliminating the use of deprecated Liquid tags. When a deprecated tag is used, the check reports the offense with the deprecation reason (if available) to help you migrate to the recommended alternative.

## Examples

The list of deprecated tags comes from the [Liquid documentation](/api-reference/liquid/introduction). When a tag is marked as deprecated there, every usage is reported with the deprecation reason and the recommended replacement (when available).

### &#x2717; Incorrect Code Example (Avoid using this):

```liquid
{% raw %}
{% hash_assign user['name'] = 'John' %}
{% endraw %}
```

The `hash_assign` tag is deprecated — the [`assign`](/api-reference/liquid/variables) tag supports the same hash assignment syntax.

### &#x2713; Correct Code Example (Use this instead):

```liquid
{% raw %}
{% assign user['name'] = 'John' %}
{% endraw %}
```

Note that the `{% raw %}{% include %}{% endraw %}` tag is **not** deprecated in platformOS (unlike Shopify Liquid): it is the supported way to run a partial in the caller's scope, e.g. helpers that redirect or set the response status of the including page. Prefer [`render`](/api-reference/liquid/include) for self-contained partials.

## Configuration

The default configuration for this check:

```yaml
DeprecatedTag:
  enabled: true
  severity: warning
```

## Disabling This Check

Use the `platformos-check-disable` comment to suppress specific instances when migrating legacy code:

```liquid
{% raw %}
{% # platformos-check-disable DeprecatedTag %}
{% hash_assign user['name'] = 'John' %}
{% # platformos-check-enable DeprecatedTag %}
{% endraw %}
```

